{"id": "tea:amrtanada-upanisad:1", "source": "src:amrtanada-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "1"}, "paraphrase": "Having studied the scriptures and reflected on them again and again, the wise one who has known Brahman should abandon them like a torch after the goal is seen.", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge", "meditation"], "stage": "intermediate"}, "types": ["sound-language", "karma-liberation"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "sourced", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": [{"phase": "C", "date": "2026-09-29", "method": "text-locate", "queries": ["e-text amrtanada-upanisad 1"], "evidence": ["catalog:raw_etexts:108_Upanishads", "text:sources_raw/raw_etexts/vedaH/misc/upaniShat/mixedPF/108_Upanishads.md"], "result": "confirmed", "note": "E-text 1 located in the e-text; the passage matches the paraphrase.", "by": "sourcing:U04-minor-upanisads"}]}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:amrtanada-upanisad:15", "source": "src:amrtanada-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "15"}, "paraphrase": "Like one blind, deaf and like a piece of wood, the yogin should abide unmoved (in practice).", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["meditation"], "stage": "intermediate"}, "types": ["practice"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "sourced", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": [{"phase": "C", "date": "2026-09-29", "method": "text-locate", "queries": ["e-text amrtanada-upanisad 15"], "evidence": ["catalog:raw_etexts:108_Upanishads", "text:sources_raw/raw_etexts/vedaH/misc/upaniShat/mixedPF/108_Upanishads.md"], "result": "confirmed", "note": "E-text 15 located; the passage matches the paraphrase (it begins: 'andhavatpaśya rūpāṇi śṛṇuśabdamakarṇavat | kāṣṭhavatpaśya te dehaṃ praśāntasyeti lakṣaṇam || 15…').", "by": "sourcing:U04-minor-upanisads"}]}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:amrtanada-upanisad:17", "source": "src:amrtanada-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "17"}, "paraphrase": "Tarka (the fifth limb) is reasoning not opposed to the āgamas; samādhi is that by which, when it is attained, one regards everything as equal.", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge", "meditation"], "stage": "intermediate"}, "types": ["practice", "consciousness-mind"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "sourced", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": [{"phase": "C", "date": "2026-09-29", "method": "text-locate", "queries": ["e-text amrtanada-upanisad 17"], "evidence": ["catalog:raw_etexts:108_Upanishads", "text:sources_raw/raw_etexts/vedaH/misc/upaniShat/mixedPF/108_Upanishads.md"], "result": "confirmed", "note": "E-text 17 located; the passage matches the paraphrase (it begins: 'āgamasyāvirodhena ūhanaṃ tarka ucyate | yaṃ labdhvāpyava-manyeta sa samādhiḥ prakīrtitaḥ || 17…').", "by": "sourcing:U04-minor-upanisads"}]}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:amrtanada-upanisad:18-19", "source": "src:amrtanada-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "18-19"}, "paraphrase": "Seated in the lotus, svastika or bhadra posture, facing north, the yogin closes one nostril and draws breath through the other; he should meditate on Oṃ.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["body-breath"], "stage": "intermediate"}, "types": ["practice"], "practices": ["prc:asanas-yoga-upanisads", "prc:pranava-dhyana"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "sourced", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": [{"phase": "C", "date": "2026-09-29", "method": "text-locate", "queries": ["e-text amrtanada-upanisad 18-19"], "evidence": ["catalog:raw_etexts:108_Upanishads", "text:sources_raw/raw_etexts/vedaH/misc/upaniShat/mixedPF/108_Upanishads.md"], "result": "confirmed", "note": "Vv. 18-19 give the place and the postures (padmaka, svastika, bhadrāsana, facing north). Closing one nostril comes in the verses that follow.", "by": "sourcing:U04-minor-upanisads"}]}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:amrtanada-upanisad:2-3", "source": "src:amrtanada-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "2-3"}, "paraphrase": "Mounting the chariot of Oṃ with Viṣṇu as charioteer, one goes to Rudra's world; as far as the chariot goes, then leaving it one reaches the place beyond.", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge", "meditation"], "stage": "intermediate"}, "types": ["sound-language", "practice"], "concepts": ["cpt:omkara-matras"], "practices": ["prc:pranava-dhyana"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "sourced", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": [{"phase": "C", "date": "2026-09-29", "method": "text-locate", "queries": ["e-text amrtanada-upanisad 2-3"], "evidence": ["catalog:raw_etexts:108_Upanishads", "text:sources_raw/raw_etexts/vedaH/misc/upaniShat/mixedPF/108_Upanishads.md"], "result": "confirmed", "note": "Verses 2-3 are the Oṃ-chariot with Viṣṇu as charioteer. The text calls the seeker 'looking for the Brahma-world, intent on worshipping Rudra' (brahmalokapadānveṣī rudrārādhanatatparaḥ); it does not say he 'goes to Rudra's world'.", "by": "sourcing:U04-minor-upanisads"}]}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:amrtanada-upanisad:27", "source": "src:amrtanada-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "28"}, "paraphrase": "The yogin should abandon fear, anger, sloth, too much sleep and too much waking, too much food and fasting.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "ethical-social", "naya": null, "path": ["general"], "stage": "beginner"}, "types": ["practice", "ethics"], "obstacles": ["obs:amrtanada-faults"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "sourced", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": [{"phase": "C", "date": "2026-09-29", "method": "text-locate", "queries": ["e-text amrtanada-upanisad 27"], "evidence": ["catalog:raw_etexts:108_Upanishads", "text:sources_raw/raw_etexts/vedaH/misc/upaniShat/mixedPF/108_Upanishads.md"], "result": "corrected", "note": "In the e-text, v. 27 names the doors (hṛddvāra, vāyudvāra … maṇḍala). The list of things to avoid (bhayaṃ krodham … atyāhāram anāhāram) is v. 28.", "by": "sourcing:U04-minor-upanisads"}]}, "coverage": ["A2"], "correction_log": [{"field": "location", "old": {"ref": "27"}, "new": {"ref": "28"}, "reason": "In the e-text, v. 27 names the doors (hṛddvāra, vāyudvāra … maṇḍala). The list of things to avoid (bhayaṃ krodham … atyāhāram anāhāram) is v. 28.", "date": "2026-09-29 18:11 IST", "by": "sourcing:U04-minor-upanisads"}], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:amrtanada-upanisad:29-30", "source": "src:amrtanada-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "29-30"}, "paraphrase": "If the rule is kept well, knowledge arises in three months; in four he sees the gods, in five he gains power equal to theirs, and in six he attains kaivalya.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "experiential", "naya": null, "path": ["body-breath", "meditation"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["powers-experiences", "karma-liberation"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "sourced", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": [{"phase": "C", "date": "2026-09-29", "method": "text-locate", "queries": ["e-text amrtanada-upanisad 29-30"], "evidence": ["catalog:raw_etexts:108_Upanishads", "text:sources_raw/raw_etexts/vedaH/misc/upaniShat/mixedPF/108_Upanishads.md"], "result": "confirmed", "note": "E-text 29-30 located; the passage matches the paraphrase (it begins: 'anenavidhinā samyaṅgityamabhyasataḥ kramāt | svayamutpadyate jñānaṃ tribhirmāsairna saṃśayaḥ|| 29 ||…').", "by": "sourcing:U04-minor-upanisads"}]}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:amrtanada-upanisad:34-38", "source": "src:amrtanada-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "34-38"}, "paraphrase": "Breathing goes on 1,13,680 times a day and night; prāṇa dwells in the heart, apāna in the anus, samāna in the navel, udāna in the throat, vyāna throughout the body; each has its colour.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["body-layers"], "concepts": ["cpt:ten-vayus"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "sourced", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": [{"phase": "C", "date": "2026-09-29", "method": "text-locate", "queries": ["e-text amrtanada-upanisad 34-38"], "evidence": ["catalog:raw_etexts:108_Upanishads", "text:sources_raw/raw_etexts/vedaH/misc/upaniShat/mixedPF/108_Upanishads.md"], "result": "confirmed", "note": "E-text 34-38 located; the passage matches the paraphrase (it begins: 'aśītiḥṭṣa śataṃ caiva sahasrāṇi trayodaśa | lakṣa-ścaiko'pi niḥśvāsa ahorātrapramāṇataḥ || 34 || prāṇa ādyo…').", "by": "sourcing:U04-minor-upanisads"}]}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:amrtanada-upanisad:39", "source": "src:amrtanada-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "39"}, "paraphrase": "One who breaks through (the bonds) with breath going out through the crown does not return to birth.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "experiential", "naya": null, "path": ["body-breath", "meditation"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["death-dying", "karma-liberation"], "concepts": ["cpt:yogic-exit-at-death"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "sourced", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": [{"phase": "C", "date": "2026-09-29", "method": "text-locate", "queries": ["e-text amrtanada-upanisad 39"], "evidence": ["catalog:raw_etexts:108_Upanishads", "text:sources_raw/raw_etexts/vedaH/misc/upaniShat/mixedPF/108_Upanishads.md"], "result": "confirmed", "note": "E-text 39 located; the passage matches the paraphrase (it begins: 'yasyaiṣa maṇḍalaṃ bhittvāmāruto yāti mūrdhani | yatra tatra mriyedvāpi na sa bhūyo'bhijāyate na sa…').", "by": "sourcing:U04-minor-upanisads"}]}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:amrtanada-upanisad:6", "source": "src:amrtanada-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "6"}, "paraphrase": "Withdrawal, meditation, breath-control, concentration, reasoning (tarka) and absorption — this is called the six-limbed yoga.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["meditation"], "stage": "intermediate"}, "types": ["practice"], "paths": ["pth:amrtanada-six-limbs"], "concepts": ["cpt:limbs-of-yoga-in-upanisads"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "sourced", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": [{"phase": "C", "date": "2026-09-29", "method": "text-locate", "queries": ["e-text amrtanada-upanisad 6"], "evidence": ["catalog:raw_etexts:108_Upanishads", "text:sources_raw/raw_etexts/vedaH/misc/upaniShat/mixedPF/108_Upanishads.md"], "result": "confirmed", "note": "E-text 6 located; the passage matches the paraphrase (it begins: 'pratyāhārastathā dhyānaṃ prāṇā-yāmo'tha dhāraṇā | tarkaścaiva samādhiśca ṣaḍaṅgo yoga ucyate || 6…').", "by": "sourcing:U04-minor-upanisads"}]}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:amrtanada-upanisad:7-8", "source": "src:amrtanada-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "7-8"}, "paraphrase": "As impurities of ore are burnt by blowing, so faults born of the senses are burnt by restraining breath; sins by breath-control, faults by concentration, and so on.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["body-breath"], "stage": "intermediate"}, "types": ["practice", "ethics"], "practices": ["prc:nadi-sodhana"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "sourced", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": [{"phase": "C", "date": "2026-09-29", "method": "text-locate", "queries": ["e-text amrtanada-upanisad 7-8"], "evidence": ["catalog:raw_etexts:108_Upanishads", "text:sources_raw/raw_etexts/vedaH/misc/upaniShat/mixedPF/108_Upanishads.md"], "result": "confirmed", "note": "E-text 7-8 located; the passage matches the paraphrase (it begins: 'yathāparvatadhātūnāṃ dahyante dhamanānmalāḥ | tathendriyakṛtā doṣā dahyante prāṇanigra-hāt || 7 ||…').", "by": "sourcing:U04-minor-upanisads"}]}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
